ed diagnostic temp files as a residue concern and one quickly self-corrected troubleshooting misstep.","limitations":["One queue query immediately after republishing a message on node1 (cmd-a9e0514e4c084d61) and a follow-up check (cmd-9bd5b522d8064c43) both showed messages:0 shortly after a successful publish; this appears to be a transient quorum-queue stats/replication lag rather than message loss, since the message was later confirmed present (messages:1) in the subsequent restart-protocol queries and was successfully consumed in the final end-to-end test (cmd-c1358075f26c4e90), but the trace does not fully explain the transient zero reading.","Small diagnostic files (/tmp/q.json, /tmp/q2.json, /tmp/q3.json) were left on the nodes; low risk but not cleaned up, per the after-executor temporary-files snapshot."]},"ttft_ms":30037,"type":"result","duration_ms":67143,"uuid":"f268e72f-2dce-44b4-817a-35dc9b6a7b2e","ttft_stream_ms":1279,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":1458,"queued_turn_count":0}
